# Line endings (issue #256): Dex verifies the exact bytes of release-owned
# files against release hashes — the installed-files manifest is bound to
# the release catalog, catalog items declare per-file payload hashes
# (.claude/skills/**), and the update journey binds source bytes under
# core/ and scripts/. Git's own recommended core.autocrlf=true on Windows
# converts text files to CRLF on checkout, which broke every such check on
# every Windows install. Force LF for Dex-shipped scopes only — NEVER a
# blanket rule: this same repo holds the user's own vault content
# (autocommitted notes, seed files like CLAUDE.md), whose bytes must round-
# trip exactly as the user wrote them through any restore or rewind.
core/**     text=auto eol=lf
scripts/**  text=auto eol=lf
.scripts/** text=auto eol=lf
docs/**     text=auto eol=lf
packages/** text=auto eol=lf
.claude/**  text=auto eol=lf
System/.installed-files.manifest text eol=lf

# User-owned areas inside covered scopes keep the user's exact bytes.
.claude/skills-custom/** -text
.claude/skills/*-custom/** -text

# This fixture's CRLF bytes are the point of its test — never convert it.
core/tests/fixtures/entity_pages/09-crlf.md -text

